  "rationales": {"U":"'Modification History After the baseline version of this document is approved' lacks subject and active agent; 'this document' is ambiguous without scope definition (e.g., which document? SRS? Design Spec?); readers cannot determine applicability without context.", "A":"'any changes made to the document must be approved in accordance with the provisions of the established Change Management Plan' contains undefined terms: 'established' (when? by whom?), 'provisions' (which ones?), and no criteria for what constitutes 'approval' (e.g., sign-off, tool-based workflow, quorum).", "C":"The requirement correctly reflects a standard configuration management practice; no factual contradiction is evident, though precision is low — it is broadly consistent with ISO/IEC/IEEE 12207 and IEEE 830 expectations for baselining.", "V":"No testable condition or observable outcome is specified: no definition of 'approved change', no measurable artifact (e.g., 'a Change Record ID shall appear in Section 5.2'), no pass/fail criterion — verification would require subjective audit, not objective test."}, 
  "suggestions": {"U":"For the Software Requirements Specification (SRS) document identified by identifier 'SRS-2024-v1.0', after its baseline approval date, each subsequent modification shall be recorded in the Modification History table (Section 1.3) and linked to an approved Change Request ID.", "A":"Each modification to the SRS document after baseline approval shall be associated with a Change Request ID that has received formal approval via the Change Control Board (CCB), as defined in Section 4.2 of the Project Change Management Plan (v2.1, dated 2024-03-15).", "C":"Keep unchanged — the core intent aligns with industry-standard baselining practice.", "V":"The SRS document shall contain a Modification History table (Section 1.3) in which every row includes: (1) Date of change, (2) Change Request ID, (3) CCB Approval Date, and (4) Name of approving CCB member; all entries with CCB Approval Date later than the baseline approval date shall have non-empty values in all four fields."},
